{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 🧠 Logistic Regression Explanation and Hands-on Example\n",
        "\n",
        "Welcome to the hands-on explanation notebook for **Logistic Regression**! In this notebook, we will:\n",
        "1. Generate a synthetic binary classification dataset based on the gauge classification case study (`analog-gauge` vs. `digital-gauge`).\n",
        "2. Train a **Logistic Regression** classifier using `scikit-learn`.\n",
        "3. Implement **Logistic Regression from scratch** using **Gradient Descent** and the **Sigmoid function**.\n",
        "4. Plot the training loss reduction over iterations.\n",
        "5. Visualize the **decision boundary** separating the two classes.\n",
        "6. Relate this back to classification heads in Deep Learning models (like YOLO).\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's start by importing the necessary libraries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set seed for reproducibility\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Case Study Data Generation\n",
        "\n",
        "We generate 100 sample gauges with two features:\n",
        "1.  `aspect_ratio` (circular gauges are circular/square: ~1.0; digital screens are wider: ~1.7)\n",
        "2.  `text_density` (digital screens have much more text/numbers printed; analog gauges have fewer ticks/digits)\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's synthesize the data:\n",
        "*   Class 1 (`analog-gauge`): aspect ratio centered at 1.0, text density centered at 2.0\n",
        "*   Class 0 (`digital-gauge`): aspect ratio centered at 1.7, text density centered at 5.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        m = 100 # number of samples\n",
        \n",
        "# Generate analog gauges (Class 1)\n",
        "X_analog = np.random.randn(m // 2, 2) * 0.2 + np.array([1.0, 2.0])\n",
        "y_analog = np.ones(m // 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate digital gauges (Class 0)\n",
        "X_digital = np.random.randn(m // 2, 2) * 0.2 + np.array([1.7, 5.5])\n",
        "y_digital = np.zeros(m // 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Combine datasets\n",
        "X = np.vstack((X_analog, X_digital))\n",
        "y = np.concatenate((y_analog, y_digital))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot the dataset\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_analog[:, 0], X_analog[:, 1], color='blue', label='Class 1: Analog Gauge', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_digital[:, 0], X_digital[:, 1], color='red', label='Class 0: Digital Gauge', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Aspect Ratio')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Text Density')\n",
        "plt.title('Gauge Classification Dataset')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Logistic Regression using Scikit-Learn\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's fit the logistic classifier and evaluate the learned coefficients."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Train sklearn model\n",
        "model = LogisticRegression()\n",
        "model.fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Retrieve coefficients\n",
        "sklearn_w1, sklearn_w2 = model.coef_[0]\n",
        "sklearn_b = model.intercept_[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Skikit-Learn parameters:\")\n",
        "print(f\"w_1 (Aspect Ratio Coefficient): {sklearn_w1:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"w_2 (Text Density Coefficient) : {sklearn_w2:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Bias (Intercept)               : {sklearn_b:.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Evaluate accuracy\n",
        "y_pred_sklearn = model.predict(X)\n",
        "print(f\"Training Accuracy: {accuracy_score(y, y_pred_sklearn) * 100:.2f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Logistic Regression from Scratch (Gradient Descent)\n",
        "\n",
        "Recall the mathematical equations.\n",
        "Sigmoid function:\n",
        "$$\\sigma(z) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-z}}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Hypothesis prediction:\n",
        "$$\\hat{y}^{(i)} = \\sigma(\\mathbf{w}^T \\mathbf{x}^{(i)} + b)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Binary Cross-Entropy Loss:\n",
        "$$J(w, b) = -\\frac{1}{m} \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\left[ y^{(i)} \\log(\\hat{y}^{(i)}) + (1 - y^{(i)}) \\log(1 - \\hat{y}^{(i)}) \\right]$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Gradients:\n",
        "$$\\frac{\\partial J}{\\partial \\mathbf{w}} = \\frac{1}{m} \\mathbf{X}^T (\\hat{\\mathbf{y}} - \\mathbf{y})$$\n",
        "$$\\frac{\\partial J}{\\partial b} = \\frac{1}{m} \\sum_{i=1}^{m} (\\hat{y}^{(i)} - y^{(i)})$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's implement this!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(z):\n",
        "    return 1 / (1 + np.exp(-z))\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_loss(y, y_pred):\n",
        "    # Add epsilon to prevent log(0) error\n",
        "    eps = 1e-15\n",
        "    y_pred = np.clip(y_pred, eps, 1 - eps)\n",
        "    return -np.mean(y * np.log(y_pred) + (1 - y) * np.log(1 - y_pred))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Hyperparameters\n",
        "learning_rate = 0.5\n",
        "epochs = 500\n",
        "m, n = X.shape\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize weights and bias\n",
        "w_custom = np.zeros(n)\n",
        "b_custom = 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "loss_history = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
        "    # 1. Forward Pass\n",
        "    z = X @ w_custom + b_custom\n",
        "    y_pred = sigmoid(z)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # 2. Compute Loss\n",
        "    loss = compute_loss(y, y_pred)\n",
        "    loss_history.append(loss)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # 3. Backward Pass\n",
        "    dw = (1 / m) * (X.T @ (y_pred - y))\n",
        "    db = np.mean(y_pred - y)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # 4. Update parameters\n",
        "    w_custom -= learning_rate * dw\n",
        "    b_custom -= learning_rate * db\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if epoch % 100 == 0:\n",
        "        print(f\"Epoch {epoch:03d} | Loss: {loss:.4f} | w: {w_custom} | b: {b_custom:.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFinal Learned Parameters (Custom Scratch):\")\n",
        "print(f\"w: {w_custom} | b: {b_custom:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Let's plot the binary cross-entropy loss reduction curve."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
        "plt.plot(loss_history, color='orange', linewidth=2)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Epoch')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Binary Cross-Entropy Loss')\n",
        "plt.title('BCE Loss Reduction Curve')\n",
        "plt.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Visualizing the Decision Boundary\n",
        "\n",
        "The decision boundary is the line where the predicted probability is exactly 0.5. This happens when the linear combination $z = 0$:\n",
        "$$w_1 x_1 + w_2 x_2 + b = 0$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Solving for $x_2$ (Text Density) to plot:\n",
        "$$x_2 = -\\frac{w_1}{w_2} x_1 - \\frac{b}{w_2}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's draw this boundary line on top of our data points!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot data points\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_analog[:, 0], X_analog[:, 1], color='blue', label='Class 1: Analog Gauge', alpha=0.6)\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_digital[:, 0], X_digital[:, 1], color='red', label='Class 0: Digital Gauge', alpha=0.6)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate X values for decision boundary line\n",
        "x_boundary = np.linspace(0.6, 2.0, 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Scikit-Learn boundary\n",
        "y_boundary_sklearn = -(sklearn_w1 / sklearn_w2) * x_boundary - (sklearn_b / sklearn_w2)\n",
        "plt.plot(x_boundary, y_boundary_sklearn, color='green', linewidth=2, label='Sklearn Decision Boundary')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Custom Scratch boundary\n",
        "y_boundary_custom = -(w_custom[0] / w_custom[1]) * x_boundary - (b_custom / w_custom[1])\n",
        "plt.plot(x_boundary, y_boundary_custom, color='purple', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label='Scratch Decision Boundary')\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Aspect Ratio')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Text Density')\n",
        "plt.title('Logistic Regression Decision Boundary Comparison')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.ylim(1.0, 6.5)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 💡 Connection to Deep Learning & YOLO\n",
        "*   **Classification Layer (Sigmoid Activation):** In multi-label object classification tasks in models like YOLO, the final bounding box class scores are calculated using **Sigmoid** activation. YOLO uses **Binary Cross-Entropy Loss** for classification, training a separate logistic regression head for each class label to predict whether the detected object contains specific features (e.g. `lever-valve` vs `control-valve`)."
      ]
    }
  ],
